<body>
    <main>
        <h1>LeetCode 3789: Minimum Cost to Acquire Required Items (C++)</h1>
        <div class="problem-description">
            <p><strong>Problem:</strong>
                You are given five integers cost1, cost2, costBoth, need1, and need2. There are three types
                of items: a type 1 item costs cost1 and counts toward need1 only, a type 2 item costs cost2
                and counts toward need2 only, and a type 3 item costs costBoth and counts toward both need1
                and need2 at the same time. You must buy items so that the total number of items counting
                toward need1 is at least need1 and the total number counting toward need2 is at least
                need2. Return the minimum total cost required to acquire the required items.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong>
                Input: cost1 = 3, cost2 = 2, costBoth = 1, need1 = 3, need2 = 2<br>
                Output: 3<br>
                Explanation: Buying three type 3 items costs 3 * 1 = 3 and satisfies both requirements
                (3 &gt;= 3 and 3 &gt;= 2). No cheaper valid combination exists.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-container">
            <button class="copy-button" onclick="copyCode(this)">Copy Code</button>
            <pre><code class="language-cpp">class Solution {
public:
    long long minimumCost(int cost1, int cost2, int costBoth, int need1, int need2) {
        auto calc = [&amp;](long long a, int x, long long b, int y) {
            int p = min(x, costBoth);
            int q = min(y, costBoth - p);
            return a * p + b * q;
        };
        return max(calc(need1, cost1, need2, cost2), calc(need2, cost2, need1, cost1));
    }
};</code></pre>
